Subject: [PATCH] net: dsa: publish the requested ageing time before notification

The switch-wide ageing calculation includes every port's cached value.
Notifying before updating the requesting port lets its old shorter value
win the minimum. After STP changes a four-port bridge from 300 seconds to
30 seconds and back, the last restoring port still keeps hardware at
30 seconds even though all cached values become 300 seconds afterward.

Publish the proposed value before the synchronous notifier and restore
the old value on error. Keep the switch-wide minimum across ports intact.

---
--- a/net/dsa/port.c
+++ b/net/dsa/port.c
@@ -877,15 +877,20 @@
 	unsigned long ageing_jiffies = clock_t_to_jiffies(ageing_clock);
 	unsigned int ageing_time = jiffies_to_msecs(ageing_jiffies);
 	struct dsa_notifier_ageing_time_info info;
+	unsigned int old_ageing_time = dp->ageing_time;
 	int err;
 
 	info.ageing_time = ageing_time;
 
+	/* The switch-wide minimum must include this port's new value, even
+	 * when it is the last port restoring a longer ageing time.
+	 */
+	dp->ageing_time = ageing_time;
 	err = dsa_port_notify(dp, DSA_NOTIFIER_AGEING_TIME, &info);
-	if (err)
+	if (err) {
+		dp->ageing_time = old_ageing_time;
 		return err;
-
-	dp->ageing_time = ageing_time;
+	}
 
 	return 0;
 }
